WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.830
Mobile Task Forces, the renowned first line
of defense for the SCP Foundation.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.630
Comprised of the organization's most highly
trained operatives, MTFs are the boots on

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.839
the ground dealing with anomalous threats
and containment breaches head-on.

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:16.990
It’s a dangerous job.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.609
In fact, joining an MTF is widely considered
one of the most hazardous roles within the

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:23.550
entire Foundation.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:29.180
One where every day brings with it a whole
host of unexpected threats… and a high number

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.180
of casualties.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.140
So let’s take a look at how one of those
days goes.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.690
6:00 AM
“Rise and shine, troops!” comes a gravel-voiced

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.129
yell louder than any alarm clock.

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:46.110
The very second that early morning call goes
out over the intercom, the members of MTF

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.219
Nu-7 are on their feet.

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:52.399
Climbing out of their bunks and quickly getting
into uniform, the operators file out of their

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.510
barracks and hastily make their way to the
mess hall.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:01.440
Among them is the latest recruit to join this
particular task force, Private Killian Hess,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.879
lines up to receive his breakfast behind his
new squad mates.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.810
This all takes place before most of the Foundation
has even woken up.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:13.100
Even though these MTF operatives would rely
on working as a team to keep each other alive,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.119
there is little casual conversation.

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:20.310
Most of them are actually quite solemn as
they eat, aware of the inherent risk that

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.000
comes with their job.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.560
Private Hess, receiving a briefing the previous
day, is paired with a more grizzled and much

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.560
older veteran of Nu-7, Lieutenant Patterson.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.329
Upon sitting down next to his new senior officer,
Hess immediately asks what has the rest of

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:37.009
the unit feeling so down.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:40.190
“Boy, you really are new,” Patterson scoffs.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.070
“Look, rookie, we do what we do and watch
each other’s backs like good soldiers.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:50.920
But make no mistake: you’re on the USS Enterprise
now, kid… and we’re the red shirts.”

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.399
8:00 AM
Following their breakfast and early start,

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:58.439
any MTF operatives that aren’t thrust into
immediate action are sent to their designated

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:00.079
basic training area.

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:04.539
Here they are presented with all manner of
intense assault courses, fighting rings for

00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:10.729
hand-to-hand sparring, and a live ammo shooting
range to improve skills with weapon proficiency.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:15.750
The SCP Foundation demands the highest level
of skill from its Mobile Task Forces, so regular

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:20.370
combat drills are an absolute necessity for
keeping their operators alert and ready to

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.690
take on all manner of threats.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:27.780
For some of the more hot-headed MTF troops,
drills are a chance to cut loose, show off

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.080
their skills or challenge their squad mates
to beat each other’s fastest assault course

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.950
times or shooting range scores.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.890
But to those that have been around longer,
and have the benefit of hindsight after multiple

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:45.099
catastrophic containment breaches, morning
training can feel like pretty inadequate preparation.

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:50.870
After all, the Foundation sends its MTFs out
to take on some of their most dangerous SCPs,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.940
most of which have wild, unpredictable abilities.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.170
How does Practising Krav Maga really help
prepare someone for a fight with a creature

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.420
that can warp reality around it?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.519
And hitting motionless paper targets at a
range can seem a little redundant when some

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:08.170
anomalies are virtually bulletproof.
10:00 AM

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.980
Of course, this is the SCP Foundation, meaning
it doesn’t take long for some strange happening

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.980
to occur.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.069
MTF Nu-7 are soon dispatched on their first
assignment, after the Foundation loses contact

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:22.680
with a site known to house a particularly
dangerous anomaly.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.409
Nicknamed ‘Hammer Down’, the task force
Hess has found himself thrust into is usually

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:33.040
deployed as a direct result of incidents where
communication is lost with Foundation facilities,

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.270
and containment breaches are suspected to
have occurred.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.390
Hopping aboard a high-speed transport, Private
Hess and the rest of Hammer Down are quickly

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.820
briefed on their mission.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.920
At approximately 0900 hours the same day,
the Foundation lost contact with another pair

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:54.439
of their MTFs – Omega-59, aka Nechayeva's
Wolves, and Sigma-18, the Chess Masters.

00:03:54.439 --> 00:04:00.400
Both were stationed at Armed Containment Complex
04, a secure location within the Russian Federation’s

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.870
Sakha Republic.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.540
Patterson informs the rest of MTF Nu-7 that
they were to re-establish communication with

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.299
the site, and assess any potential danger.

00:04:09.299 --> 00:04:14.069
Although, by the time the transport arrives
at Complex 04, it becomes pretty clear that

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:16.579
things aren’t looking good.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:21.870
SCP-1984 has breached containment: the Dead
Hand is loose.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:28.169
Unluckily for Hammer Down, SCP-1984 is a semi-corporeal
entity with the nasty habit of attacking any

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:33.080
human being that it comes into contact with,
by disrupting their nervous systems, usually

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.740
resulting in excruciating pain.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:39.740
Although that did answer the question of what
had happened to the other MTFs at the site…

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.430
12:00 PM
Immediately engaging the Dead Hand, Hammer

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.580
Down stormed Complex 04.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.340
Patterson had ordered them to go weapons hot
on the creature from the moment the transport

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.620
touched down.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:56.530
Having manifested as a hazy, humanoid outline,
SCP-1984 was making quick work of slaughtering

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.620
MTF Omega-59 and Sigma-18.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:04.220
Nu-7 were able to intercept before it could
completely decimate their fellow operatives,

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:08.940
but now the Dead Hand had them pinned, stopping
the unit from accessing the on-site armory.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:13.449
While they had all arrived loaded for bear,
the MTF operatives knew they couldn’t keep

00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:18.729
SCP-1984 at bay for long with only their standard-issue
conventional weapons.

00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:24.080
The entity’s only known weakness was microwave
radiation that could be emitted using specialized

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.520
weapons, if only they could access the Complex
04 armory.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:33.520
Time is of the essence too, and the pressure
of stopping SCP-1984 quickly weighs heavily

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.010
on Private Hess.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:39.310
He and the rest of Hammer Down know how the
entity operates, that it would be heading

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.319
just over eighty kilometers northwest at the
first chance it got.

00:05:43.319 --> 00:05:48.220
If one too many of them were killed, or there
was a pause in the fighting for a second too

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:52.819
long, the Dead Hand would be on its way to
an installation nearby housing a number of

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:55.250
Intercontinental Ballistic Missiles.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:00.350
Once there, it would waste no time, interfacing
with nuclear command systems, launching those

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:04.170
ICBMs, and causing catastrophic destruction.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.390
1:30 PM
Deploying some quick thinking, Lieutenant

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:12.530
Patterson contacted Foundation command, and
had them send a secondary detachment of Nu-7

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.100
to the missile installation.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:19.000
Part of their Mobile Task Force includes a
platoon of experts in various forms of warfare,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.349
not just chemical and biological, but nuclear
too.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:26.520
While that portion of Hammer Down were directed
to lock down the missile installation eighty

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:33.810
kilometers away, Patterson, Hess, and the
rest of Nu-7 were trying to distract SCP-1984.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.530
Their engagement lasted around an hour, with
the entity attacking a number of the troops

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.750
on the ground.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.889
Each one would suffer symptoms of intense
neurological trauma, including seizures and

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:46.620
the loss of cerebral spinal fluid from their
nose and eyes.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.620
Experiencing it was painful enough, and the
sight of his fellow MTF agents dying in such

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.600
a horrific fashion wasn’t exactly what Private
Hess expected from his first day.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:01.910
Eventually, SCP-1984 dissipates after a sustained
battle with Hammer Down, although it could

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:05.410
easily remanifest if it ever intercepts particular
broadcasts.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:10.310
But the task forces’ work at Complex 04
is far from over.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.900
After the battle comes the clean-up operation.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:16.830
Private Hess follows orders from Patterson
to clear as much debris and as many bodies

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:21.660
as he can, making a note of every member of
their unit that they lost to the Dead Hand.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:26.520
However, it doesn’t take long for the surviving
members of Nu-7 to receive another call for

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.520
assistance.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.330
4:00 PM
Despite Hess’ concerns that he and the others

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:35.150
haven’t eaten in hours, the team loads up
and heads out again.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:38.680
The Foundation has sent word that someone
has taken advantage of all the commotion at

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:43.110
Complex 04, and forced their way into a different
site.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:47.740
Wasting no time, the remainder of Hammer Down
dusted off from the Sakha Republic, locking

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.110
and loading, ready to begin their next mission.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:56.099
Arriving at the site, Foundation command radios
to Nu-7, updating them about the situation.

00:07:56.099 --> 00:08:01.050
A large group of assailants, all members of
the Church of the Broken God, was midway through

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:04.240
launching an assault against the SCP Foundation.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:09.050
Their goal was unclear, although the site
they had targeted was known to house SCP-882.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:15.009
This anomaly is widely believed to be the
heart of the Broken God, a deity worshipped

00:08:15.009 --> 00:08:17.430
by those of the Mekhanist faith.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:22.169
One of the Church’s core goals was to repair
their god, as well as to enhance themselves

00:08:22.169 --> 00:08:24.710
through mechanical, anomalous means.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:29.759
Of course, this meant that a group of cyborg
cultists awaited the arriving task force.

00:08:29.759 --> 00:08:33.719
Hammer Down clashes with the Church of the
Broken God, trying to divert them away from

00:08:33.719 --> 00:08:37.769
the saltwater tank containing SCP-882.

00:08:37.769 --> 00:08:41.620
Lieutenant Patterson warns them not to get
too close to the mass of welded metal, noting

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:46.870
that if the MTF troops’ weapons would become
fused to SCP-882.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:51.470
Hearing that is what gives Hess the idea to
engage the cyborgs hand to hand.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:55.260
Although the Church members were much stronger,
luring them closer to the heart of the Broken

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:01.360
God meant all their metallic enhancements
would also be pulled into SCP-882, killing

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:06.870
the devoted cultists, despite how pleased
they were to become one with their god, Mekhane.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.480
7:00 PM
Moments of levity are often rare for Mobile

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.769
Task Forces.

00:09:11.769 --> 00:09:17.020
Already it’s been a hell of a day, multiple
deployments and extremely high casualties.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:22.180
For Private Hess, exhaustion is already setting
in; he’s been awake for over twelve hours,

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:27.050
barely survived encounters with a hostile
SCP and a tenacious Group of Interest.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:31.320
And during each of the ensuing battles, he
has been made to watch as a number of his

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.730
fellow operatives die, some of them he’d
only just met.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.770
Now he can barely recall their names.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:42.630
Instead, as the day draws to a close, he prays
that he, Lieutenant Patterson, and the dwindling

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:48.000
remains of their squad won’t be called on
again… but this is the SCP Foundation, after

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.000
all.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.880
8:00 PM
And whatever can go wrong, usually does – with

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.120
a gigantic, angry reptile in the middle of
it.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:00.870
Sure enough, the alarms begin to sound, and
Private Hess has to get back to his feet.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:05.880
He musters what fading scraps of energy he
can will back into his being, his weapon feeling

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:08.000
heavier than it has all day.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.950
A tiny spike of adrenaline hits as Patterson
barks the fateful words Hess had hoped he

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:16.670
would never hear:
“On your feet, soldier!

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.290
SCP-682 is loose!”

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.830
Hammer Down races through the facility corridors,
passed by a flood of researchers all fleeing

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.110
for their lives.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:30.370
The MTF team reaches the containment chamber,
just in time to witness SCP-682 – the infamous

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:34.801
Hard to Destroy Reptile – lunging at the
unfortunate personnel that couldn’t get

00:10:34.801 --> 00:10:36.560
away in time.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:41.080
Right next to Hess, one of his fellow Nu-7
teammates steps in a puddle of acid that has

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.620
spilled from the vat that usually houses the
murderous reptilian monster.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:51.380
As the carnivorous SCP-682 finishes decimating
its previous target, it turns to angrily charge

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:56.870
for the MTF troops, who raise their weapons
and open fire, in what is ultimately a futile

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:00.670
attempt at stopping a creature that can’t
be harmed by mere bullets.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:03.760
10:00 PM
Hours pass.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:09.120
Containment breaches by SCP-682 are far from
an uncommon occurrence, and fortunately, the

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.300
Foundation’s task forces are more than used
to driving the creature back into its acid

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:16.010
tank, where it’s held only slightly more
securely.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:20.430
But, with every escape attempt by the Hard
to Destroy Reptile comes a slew of casualties

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.490
from Foundation personnel.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.950
And today is no exception.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:29.180
Despite having sustained heavy injuries himself,
Lieutenant Patterson is instructed by his

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.680
superiors to file an end-of-day report before
he – and those that are still breathing

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.400
– can be debriefed.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:39.550
The MTF lieutenant tallies up the considerable
losses his unit sustained on their various

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:44.140
engagements throughout the day, every operative
killed by the Dead Hand, then those that the

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.480
Church of the Broken God were able to make
quick work of, and of course, the ones who

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:54.610
met their demise at the hands – or rather
the jaws – of SCP-682.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:58.690
The role of a Mobile Task Force operative
is a difficult and dangerous job.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.620
But what few realize is how expendable these
troops are to the Foundation.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:07.040
In fact, they’re not all that different
from D Class in that regard.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.570
The SCP Foundation will simply throw their
most skilled agents into the fray, in the

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:16.320
hopes that enough of them will kill or contain
an anomalous threat no matter how many lives

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.560
it costs.

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:22.269
Perhaps nothing exemplifies that more than
the body of Private Killian Hess being wheeled

00:12:22.269 --> 00:12:27.050
away for disposal after falling in the battle
with 682.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:32.070
As if dying on his first day wasn’t bad
enough, the superior officers of MTF Nu-7

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:35.650
are already looking for a replacement to join
Hammer Down.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:39.010
If this sounds like fun to you, apply today!

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:44.050
Now then, rookie, go and check out “SCP
ELITE MOBILE TASK FORCE EXPLAINED” and “How

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:48.670
to Work at the SCP Foundation Explained”
for more of the ins and outs of working for

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:49.690
the SCP Foundation!

